  "description": "POBFIX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H78 Gd6 N12 O28 4+,2(C1 H4 O1),8(H2 O1),4(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.674-4.007 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.18-114.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C66H102Cl4Gd6N12O38. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
